WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:12.600
Friday, six in the evening. Rani has been busy all week, and nothing that matters has moved.

2
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.500
She answered every ping and joined every meeting. Her certification practice got zero hours.

3
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:27.600
Urgency is a sensation, not a measure of value. Important work never taps you on the shoulder.

4
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:34.500
Sort any week into four boxes. First: urgent and important. Real deadlines, real crises.

5
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:40.600
Second: important, not urgent. Practice, planning, people, health. Careers are built here.

6
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:45.500
Third: urgent, not important. Most pings and many meetings.

7
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.500
Fourth: neither.

8
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:56.200
The trap: box three dresses up as box one, and eats the hours box two needed.

9
00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:03.500
The defence is a weekly preview. Twenty minutes, three moves. Review where you are going.

10
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:10.000
Choose two or three important blocks, and put them in the calendar first.

11
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:16.500
Then preview the known deadlines, so they get space instead of an all-nighter.

12
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:23.400
A calendar block needs one more defence: a rehearsed no. Not a fake maybe.

13
00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:28.700
A fake maybe becomes a yes delivered late and badly.

14
00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:36.000
A graceful no has three parts: thanks, the reason you are protecting, and an alternative.

15
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:42.900
The next Thursday, seven in the evening. The pings still arrive. The block holds.

16
00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:50.200
Every yes is an unpriced no to something else. Price it before you give it.

17
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.700
Important work never taps you. Schedule it first.

18
00:01:54.700 --> 00:02:00.000
Defend it with a calendar block and a rehearsed no.

19
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.300
Now it is your turn. Book twenty minutes this weekend for your first weekly preview.
